  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Prevention of Trafficking in Persons and Other Protection Risks of Vulnerable Conflict-Affected Men, Women, Boys and Girls in Ukraine</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through this project, IOM aims to scale up its protection response, deploying IOM protection field staff in several locations and bolstering the capacity of local non-governmental organizations (NGOs). IOM and partners will also sensitize other key stakeholders carrying a shared responsibility for the protection of vulnerable populations, including national and international humanitarian actors and government officials. Sensitization will focus on protection and prevention core concepts, including referral processes for persons with protection needs, such as survivors of trafficking. IOM and its partner NGOs will engage the community through awareness activities to prevent human trafficking and mitigate other protection risks and threats, targeting some 10,000 individuals. Through case management services, IOM and partners will directly assist some 500 conflict-affected men, women, boys and girls who have experienced or are at high risk of human trafficking, gender-based violence, conflict-related sexual violence, and other forms of harm.</narrative>
  </description>
